\f1\b \cf0 Performance Goals
\f0\b0 \
\

\f1\b 1. Develop proficiency in ATP sampling and weighting
\f0\b0 \

\f1\b Goal:
\f0\b0  Develop a strong working knowledge of the American Trends Panel (ATP) sampling, weighting, and quality-checking processes, and progressively take ownership of sampling and weighting tasks.\

\f1\b Success looks like:
\f0\b0  Independently execute and validate assigned sampling and weighting tasks, identify and troubleshoot potential issues, and maintain accurate and reproducible workflows and documentation.\
\

\f1\b 2. Build expertise in Pew\'92s R-based survey methodology workflows
\f0\b0 \

\f1\b Goal:
\f0\b0  Build on my existing R proficiency to become familiar with and contribute to Pew\'92s R-based survey methodology workflows.\

\f1\b Success looks like:
\f0\b0  Become proficient in Pew\'92s existing R workflows, write reproducible code, and contribute custom functions, maintenance and improvements to tools and packages such as 
\fs24 pewmethods
\fs26 .\
\

\f1\b 3. Contribute to ATP survey operations and quality assurance
\f0\b0 \

\f1\b Goal:
\f0\b0  Develop familiarity with the ATP survey production process and contribute to survey program testing, data-quality checks, and production support. \

\f1\b Success looks like:
\f0\b0  Develop a strong understanding of the ATP production timeline and workflow; conduct thorough and timely quality checks; identify and troubleshoot programming or data-quality issues; and communicate effectively with operations and SSRS to support timely and accurate survey production.\
\

\f1\b 4. Provide methodological and analytical support to research teams
\f0\b0 \

\f1\b Goal:
\f0\b0  Provide methodological and analytical support to research teams, including data-quality investigations, analyses required for research products (such as trend analyses) timely and accurately.\

\f1\b Success looks like:
\f0\b0  Communicate analytical techniques and decisions clearly, provide methodological recommendations and work collaboratively with research teams to develop solutions, and contribute to research products and methodological documentation. \
